tle":"Finding Incompatible Blocks for Reliable JPEG Steganalysis","title_zh":"","year":2024,"publication_date":"","abstract":"","authors":[{"id":"author-01a5ce290a5efe","name":"Etienne Levecque","orcid":"0009-0008-9268-5436","institution_ids":[]},{"id":"author-0e3271efbc011c","name":"Jan Butora","orcid":"0000-0002-2540-1420","institution_ids":[]},{"id":"author-c20771801dd39c","name":"Patrick Bas","orcid":"","institution_ids":[]}],"institution_ids":[],"venue":{"id":"venue-f69a9dd74f3931","name":"IEEE Transactions on Information Forensics and Security","short_name":"TIFS","type":"journal","issn":"1556-6013","rankings":[{"system":"CAS","level":"1","category":"计算机科学","scope":"大类","is_top":true,"version":"2025","source_url":"https://www.iikx.com/sci/technology/13028.html","verified_at":"2026-08-12"},{"system":"JCR","level":"Q1","category":"Computer Science; Engineering","scope":"","is_top":false,"version":"2026","source_url":"https://www.iikx.com/sci/technology/13028.html","verified_at":"2026-08-12"}]},"task_tags":["image_steganalysis"],"contribution_type":"analysis","review_status":"verified","doi":"10.1109/tifs.2024.3470650","arxiv_id":"","openalex_id":"","semantic_scholar_id":"","primary_url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/tifs.2024.3470650","citation_count":1,"provenance":[{"source":"crossref","source_id":"10.1109/tifs.2024.3470650","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/tifs.2024.3470650","query":"image steganalysis IEEE Transactions on Information Forensics and Security TIFS","retrieved_at":"2026-07-16T04:07:46Z"}],"notes":"快速批量核验：具有稳定来源，且任务标签与图像取证范围一致。"},{"id":"paper-072ca36889e25ac0","title":"A GAN-based Approach to Detect AI-Generated Images","title_zh":"","year":2023,"publication_date":"2023-07-05","abstract":"The ease with which deep learning can generate fake images has created a pressing need for a robust platform to distinguish between real and fake imagery. However, existing methods in image forensics rely on complex deep learning architectures that are expensive to train and have limited usability due to their large model size. This study examines the difficulty of detecting state-of-the-art image manipulations, both manually and automatically. We introduce G-JOB GAN, a machine learning model based on Generative Adversarial Networks (GAN), which generates highly realistic images and achieves a 95.7% accuracy in detecting realistic generated images. The same architecture of G-JOB Gan can also detect fake images with a similar probability. To verify the results, we compare our results to several similar GAN architectures, including Style GAN, Pro GAN, and the Original GAN. Our model outperforms other GAN models in term of detection accuracy.","authors":[{"id":"author-2f8a235decebae","name":"Galamo Monkam","orcid":"","institution_ids":[]},{"id":"author-459e9c1b5a4fb6","name":"Weifeng Xu","orcid":"","institution_ids":[]},{"id":"author-674c6051b2a356","name":"Jie Yan","orcid":"","institution_ids":[]}],"institution_ids":["i324100","i6059380","institution:85dd03b724084b02","institution:86acee6f855e6b06"],"venue":{"id":"venue-eb998888e4b7b3","name":"2023 26th ACIS International Winter Conference on Software Engineering, Artificial Intelligence, Networking and Parallel/Distributed Computing (SNPD-Winter)","short_name":"","type":"conference","issn":"","rankings":[]},"task_tags":["image_forgery","synthetic_detection"],"contribution_type":"method","review_status":"verified","doi":"10.1109/snpd-winter57765.2023.10223798","arxiv_id":"","openalex_id":"W4386214843","semantic_scholar_id":"","primary_url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/snpd-winter57765.2023.10223798","citation_count":12,"provenance":[{"source":"authorized_seed","source_id":"","url":"https://openalex.org/W4386214843","query":"","retrieved_at":"2026-07-15T00:00:00Z"},{"source":"openalex","source_id":"W4386214843","url":"https://openalex.org/W4386214843","query":"GAN image forensics","retrieved_at":"2026-07-16T03:56:55Z"},{"source":"semantic_scholar","source_id":"3797a923d26dbdc7eabe34b62aae29e2eaaba07a","url":"https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/3797a923d26dbdc7eabe34b62aae29e2eaaba07a","query":"fake image detection generative AI","retrieved_at":"2026-07-15T18:32:35Z"}],"notes":"快速批量核验：已有稳定来源，且现有任务标签与图像取证范围一致。"},{"id":"paper-b9bdee847eb25ec0","title":"Heuristic Optimization Algorithm Based Watermarking on Content Authentication and Tampering Detection for English Text","title_zh":"","year":2023,"publication_date":"2023-01-01","abstract":"Text information is a natural language dependent, which enhances reliability and security of text data exchanged through Internet networks and is becoming main concern for researchers. Content authentication, Tampering detection, and integrity verification of digital content are considered challenges in the information and communication exchange area through the Internet. Watermarking algorithms emerge as a potential method for achieving this with text. In simple words, text watermarking is embedding imperceptible text messages within the content that serve as unique signatures or identifiers. The text message has data regarding the content creator, copyright data, or other metadata utilized for authentication purposes. Therefore, this study presents a new Coyote Optimization Algorithm with Watermarking-based Content Authentication and Tampering Detection (COAW-CATD) technique for English text. The presented COAW-CATD technique aims to secure the English text via content authentication and tampering recognition. To accomplish this, the presented COAW-CATD technique designs a zero-watermarking (ZWM) approach to produce watermarks depending on the textual content. The generated watermark can be extracted to assure the authentication of the text document. Moreover, the COA can be utilized to optimize the placement of the watermarks in the content to ensure that it is imperceptible and robust to tampering. The experimental outcomes of the COAW-CATD algorithm are tested utilizing a series of simulations and the comparative study reported its superior performance with improved tampering detection accuracy of 95.93%.","authors":[{"id":"a5043871968","name":"Fahd N. Al‐Wesabi","orcid":"0000-0002-4389-4927","institution_ids":["i82952536"]},{"id":"a5063985986","name":"Fadwa Alrowais","orcid":"0000-0002-8447-198X","institution_ids":["i106778892"]},{"id":"a5040941339","name":"Heba G. Mohamed","orcid":"0000-0002-0443-1049","institution_ids":["i106778892"]},{"id":"a5084632396","name":"Mesfer Al Duhayyim","orcid":"0000-0003-4024-271X","institution_ids":["i142608572"]},{"id":"a5091747108","name":"Anwer Mustafa Hilal","orcid":"0000-0002-4658-8941","institution_ids":["i142608572"]},{"id":"a5068423119","name":"Abdelwahed Motwakel","orcid":"0000-0003-4084-5457","institution_ids":["i142608572"]}],"institution_ids":["i106778892","i142608572","i82952536"],"venue":{"id":"venue-fd59544560a7dc","name":"IEEE Access","short_name":"","type":"journal","issn":"","rankings":[]},"task_tags":["image_forgery"],"contribution_type":"method","review_status":"verified","doi":"10.1109/access.2023.3297263","arxiv_id":"","openalex_id":"W4385128078","semantic_scholar_id":"","primary_url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/access.2023.3297263","citation_count":7,"provenance":[{"source":"openalex","source_id":"W4385128078","url":"https://openalex.org/W4385128078","query":"document image text tampering detection","retrieved_at":"2026-07-15T06:11:49Z"},{"source":"crossref","source_id":"10.1109/access.2023.3297263","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/access.2023.3297263","query":"scene text tampering detection localization","retrieved_at":"2026-07-16T07:30:52Z"}],"notes":"快速批量核验：已有稳定来源，且现有任务标签与图像取证范围一致。"},{"id":"paper-b48d485fee369ec0","title":"Robust zero-watermarking algorithm for diffusion-weighted images based on multiscale feature fusion","title_zh":"","year":2023,"publication_date":"","abstract":"","authors":[{"id":"author-d445c27d5b6964","name":"Zhangyu Liu","orcid":"","institution_ids":[]},{"id":"author-bf73502baec697","name":"Zh